 ## Overview
-Progressive Inpainting-and-Erasing (PERF) is a method for reconstructing a panoramic Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) from a single input panorama by iteratively expanding the viewpoint coverage. It solves the problem of geometry conflict between visible regions (observed in reference views) and invisible regions (occluded or unseen) by computing a mask of conflicted areas and eliminating them from the NeRF training supervision [S1]. Unlike methods that rely on multiple input views or semantic priors, PERF generates novel views via inpainting and progressively integrates them while erasing geometrically inconsistent pixels to ensure 3D consistency [S1].
+Progressive Inpainting-and-Erasing (PERF) is a method for reconstructing a panoramic Neural Radiance Field (NeRF) from a single input panorama by iteratively expanding the viewpoint coverage [S1]. It solves the problem of geometry conflict between visible regions (observed in reference views) and invisible regions (occluded or unseen) by computing a mask of conflicted areas and eliminating them from the NeRF training supervision [S1]. Unlike methods that rely on multiple input views or semantic priors, PERF generates novel views via inpainting and progressively integrates them while erasing geometrically inconsistent pixels to ensure 3D consistency [S1].
 
